WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:04.100
Roughly 9% of the rubbish we collect could
be recycled instead.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:08.420
Let’s take a closer look at how we use the
recycling bin.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:15.840
Everything you put into the bin, should be
clean and loose, not in a bag.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:19.020
Lids and tops from bottles and jars should
be removed.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.420
If they’re plastic, they should go in the rubbish

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:26.019
but any scrap metal can be recycled at Southbrook Resource Recovery Park.

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:30.860
Other items that can’t be accepted include
broken glass, milk or juice cartons

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:34.940
also known as Tetrapak, polystyrene and soft plastics.

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:38.820
Soft plastics include anything that you can easily scrunch up in your hand,

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:43.520
this includes bubble wrap, food wrap, chip packets and plastic bags.

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:48.320
Nappies should go into your rubbish and food soiled
cardboard like pizza boxes,

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:52.060
or napkins should go into your organics bin for composting.

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:54.420
So what should go into recycling?

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:55.860
Glass bottles and jars.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.960
Bottles and containers made from plastic
types one through to seven.

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:01.960
Tins, cans and aerosols.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:04.640
And loose, clean, flat cardboard and paper.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:13.520
To learn more or to sign up for collection
reminders visit waimakariri.govt.nz/rethinkrubbish

